      "trigger": "The 10Y sits ~4.58% — the middle of the 4.00-4.90% band — after the cool June CPI (14-Jul) rallied the front end and eased it back from ~4.63%, comfortably below its proven 5% ceiling. The regime that boxes it holds from both sides: the softer CPI and a Fed on hold (band 3.50-3.75%, no cuts priced until 2027) anchor against a runaway break through 5%, while a still ~60%-priced September hike and the July oil spike (Brent ~$86, not yet in the data) keep it from rallying under 4% — exactly the boxed-in tape a range accrual is paid to harvest, with the yield now sitting cleanly inside the band.",
